  "theorem": {
    "certificate_payload": [
      "finite slope encoding z",
      "nonzero kernel vector ell for H(u+zv)",
      "normalization degree of L(X)",
      "remainder of L(X) against X^512-1, or divisor proof",
      "the recurrence vector H(u+zv)ell",
      "the noncontainment vector H(v)ell"
    ],
    "noncontainment_gate": "The support-wise finite-affine noncontainment condition is H_{t,j}(v) ell != 0.  If H(v)ell=0 as well as H(u+zv)ell=0, then also H(u)ell=0 and the witness is in the same-support contained branch.",
    "null_polynomial_equivalence": "For a finite slope z and s_m(z)=u_m+zv_m, rank H_{t,j}(s(z))<=j iff there is a nonzero polynomial L(X)=ell_0+...+ell_j X^j such that sum_{b=0}^j s_{a+b}(z) ell_b=0 for every 0<=a<t.",
    "regular_root_interpretation": "In a nonsingular regular bucket, the v10 finite canonical roots are exactly the finite slopes admitting such a nonzero ambient null-polynomial.",
    "safe_upper_bound": "Therefore an ambient regular root table is a safe upper bound for split-locator bad slopes, and future packets may filter listed roots by the divisor and noncontainment gates.",
    "split_locator_gate": "An ambient null-polynomial gives an exact-A split locator only after normalization to a monic degree-j divisor of X^512-1."
  },
